'''Saleucami''', a name that translated into "'''oasis'''," was a [[planet]] located in the [[Saleucami system]], within the [[Suolriep sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], its inhabitants wished to stay out of the conflict, though [[Battle of Saleucami|war]] would eventually reach the backwater planet. Although [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[Grand Army of the Republic|forces]] were able to drive the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]] from Saleucami, it became the site of an [[Invasion of Saleucami|invasion]] and one of the [[Siege of Saleucami|final battles]] of the war. [[Jedi Master]] [[Stass Allie]] was killed on her [[BARC speeder]] bike by [[Clone Marshal Commander]] [[Neyo]] at the start of the [[Great Jedi Purge]].

==Description==
Saleucami was a [[Temperature|temperate]] world with a mix of environments including arid<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> [[desert]]s and [[swamp]]s.<ref name="Saleucami" /> Its name meant "oasis."<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" />

==History==
===Early history===
Around [[6000 BBY]], Saleucami was colonized by members of the [[Wroonian]] [[species]].<ref name="BMF 44" />

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Saleucami has fallen, and Master Vos moved his troops to Boz Pity.|Obi-Wan Kenobi to Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" />}}
[[File:Saleiucami_landscape.png|thumb|left|250px|The tree-covered landscape of Saleucami]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], the settlers who lived on Saleucami hoped to avoid the war.<ref name="Saleucami" /> [[clone trooper]] [[Cut Lawquane]] and his [[gunship]] crashed on Saleucami. There, Cut deserted from the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] when the [[battle droid]]s executed his fellow [[trooper]]s and fled. Cut then married [[Suu Lawquane]], made a [[Lawquane's Farm|home]] for them and her two children there.<ref name="The Deserter" />

[[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Confederate]] [[General]] [[Grievous]] and his [[fleet]] went to Saleucami along with his [[prisoner]], [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Eeth Koth]]. There, Grievous awaited the arrival of [[Jedi General]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]]. While Kenobi [[Battle of Saleucami|fought]] Grievous, Skywalker and [[Adi Gallia]] rescued Koth from Grievous's [[Grievous's Recusant-class light destroyer|''Recusant''-class light destroyer]]. Despite Skywalker and Gallia rescuing Koth, Grievous was able to escape from his [[Lightsaber duel|duel]] with Kenobi. Grievous and his forces then attempted to land, but debris from Kenobi's [[Arquitens-class light cruiser]] caused him and his battle [[droid]]s to crash-land in Saleucami's wetlands aboard a [[C-9979 landing craft]]'s [[escape pod]]s. Grievous and what remained of his forces then regrouped and searched for intact escape pods. Kenobi landed several detachments of the [[212th Attack Battalion|212th Battalion]] and [[501st Legion]] to find Grievous.<ref name="Grievous Intrigue">{{TCW|Grievous Intrigue}}</ref>

While Kenobi and Cody took the [[All Terrain Tactical Enforcer|AT-TEs]] to find the escape pods, [[Rex]] and his men then took their [[BARC speeder]]s through the wetlands. They then came under attack by two [[BX-series droid commando|droid commando]] [[sniper]]s. Rex was badly wounded and his men had to leave at the Lawquane farmstead. It was there Rex met Cut and believed that he should turn him in for desertion. However, after Cut's family and home came under attack by droid [[commando]]s, Rex decided to leave him with his family and not report him. Kenobi on the other hand, was unable to capture Grievous when he found an escape pod and made his escape.<ref name="The Deserter" /> The [[B1-series battle droid]] [[R0-GR]] was also involved in the battle, which he recalled as causing five agonizing [[Standard month|months]].<ref name="Droidography">''[[Star Wars: Droidography]]''</ref> At some point, the enhanced clones of [[Clone Force 99]]&mdash;[[Hunter]], [[Wrecker]], [[Crosshair|CT-9904]] "Crosshair," and [[Tech]]&mdash;visited Lawquane.<ref name="Cut and Run" />

The [[91st Mobile Reconnaissance Corps]] and [[Commander]] [[Mekedrix]] were involved in another [[Battle of Saleucami (Mekedrix)|battle of Saleucami]].<ref name="Obi-Wan 4">[[Obi-Wan 4|''Obi-Wan'' 4]]</ref> Upon uncovering a Separatist plan, Kenobi proposed moving Republic forces through the [[Anoat system]] and then to Saleucami.<ref name="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much">{{TCW|The Jedi Who Knew Too Much}}</ref> Saleucami eventually found itself in the thick of the war.<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> The Separatists launched<ref name="Collapse">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> an [[invasion of Saleucami]], which the [[smuggler]] [[Has Obitt]] narrowly missed.<ref name="Catalyst" /> A world nominally under the Confederacy's control, it was nevertheless valuable to the Separatists, making [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] dub it a part of the [[Triad of Evil]].<ref name="BTM 44">{{BuildFalconCite|44|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> When the [[Siege of Saleucami]] occurred during the [[Outer Rim Sieges]]<ref name="Revenge of the Sith">{{Film|III}}</ref> over the secret projects the CIS was rumored to be running on world,<ref name="Battles" /> the lengthy campaign resulted in a Republic victory towards the end of the war.<ref name="BTM 44" /> When [[Darth Sidious]] initiated [[Order 66]], [[Clone Marshal Commander]] [[Neyo]] killed [[Jedi Master]] [[Stass Allie]] while they patrolled the planet on [[BARC speeder]]s.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" />

===Imperial rule===
{{Quote|The war is over. With peace comes opportunity and prosperity for all.|Vice Admiral Rampart, via [[Hologram|holographic]] message|<ref name="Cut and Run" />}}
[[File:SaleucamiTownCheckpoint-CaR.png|thumb|right|275px|Cut in the new Imperial spaceport]]
Shortly after the [[Galactic Empire]] was [[Proclamation of the New Order|formed]], even after the war itself had finished, the clone troopers remained on Saleucami instead of pulling out, enforcing the control of the newly-established Empire,<ref name="Cut and Run" /> which was interested in Saleucami.<ref name="Cut Lawquane">{{Databank|cut-lawquane|Cut Lawquane}}</ref> Citizens found themselves forced to register for [[chain code]]s and had their [[starship]]s taken away by [[Clone impound vessel|impound vessels]]. In order to get offworld on a ship, citizens needed to register for a chain code.<ref name="Cut and Run" />

Around the same time, Rex visited Lawquane to tell him what had happened. As the [[Imperial Military]] began to lock down Saleucami, Lawquane planned to move his family off of the planet before he was discovered as a defector. The day after Rex departed, Clone Force 99 arrived. Introducing Cut to their new companions, [[Echo|CT-1409]] "Echo" and [[Omega]], Hunter wanted to learn how Cut had stayed hidden so well, as his squad were fugitives. However, their mission quickly turned into helping the family escape the planet before they were discovered.<ref name="Cut and Run" /> Saleucami was also the [[homeworld]] of Sergeant [[Warda Gojun]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[71st GAV Battalion]].<ref name="Ultimate Visual Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
Although the booklet "[[Mustafar and Other Planets in the Outer Rim]]" stated that Saleucami returned to its uninteresting status when the Clone Wars ended and the Empire rose,<ref name="Mustafar and Other Outer Rim Planets">{{EncyclopediaCite|Mustafar and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> the [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] had previously established the Empire was interested in the planet<ref name="Cut Lawquane" /> and tried to bring it under control,<ref name="Saleucami" /> with "[[Cut and Run]]" showing that the Empire took marshal control of Saleucami directly after the war ended.<ref name="Cut and Run" /> This article assumes "Mustafar and Other Outer Rim Planets" is incorrect.

